  "hypothesis": "Declarative optional/required map-character readers disagree on NUL-terminated prefixes, including optional empty-prefix defaults.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Five tested fields use the C prefix; leading-NUL initializer fields use their respective defaults. Thirteen targets accept with deterministic terrain outputs; fifteen controls cover acceptance/default/error/nonmatch boundaries.",
  "observedBehavior": "JS rejects all13 NUL-bearing targets and retains initialROOM25; exact C accepts and paintsTREE13 or the defaultROOM25/STONE0. All15 controls match.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "production_api",
    "scope": "Five explicit declarative field paths: level_init fg/bg/filling and replace_terrain fromterrain/toterrain, with per-path target/control receipts and source hashes.",
    "limitations": [
      "Five explicit field paths only: level_init fg/filling with solidfill, level_init bg with mazegrid, replace_terrain fromterrain/toterrain on the single interior cell14,10 at chance100. Default frame1,0 and no room. Snapshot compares acceptance and cell terrain, not complete map/lighting/metadata or all init styles.",
      "C executes exact wrappers/readers, actual dupstr/strlen, exact char2typ table, fill/terrain writers and seven selection helpers. Fixed typed Lua adapters preserve all string bytes, distinguish absent field from empty string, and emulate only supplied integer/enum fields. Coordinate adapter asserts the fixed single-cell rectangle and default frame. No new Lua runtime or general coercion/callback semantics claim.",
      "For replace_terrain, fixed legal rn2(100)=0 at chance100 preserves the always-successful decision; no independent RNG implementation/consumption claim. No mapfragment branch is invoked: empty fromterrain and missing fromterrain remain untested. Unused mapfragment, parser, selection-reader, callback and runtime-effect adapters abort.",
      "Initial ROOM state is created by actual solidfill on both sides. Thirteen targets preserve raw hex input in the C allocation. Fifteen controls separately test plain-char acceptance, empty optional default, multi-character rejection and a nonmatching fromterrain. Invalid controls are parser boundaries, not explained-negative setup claims.",
      "Leading-NUL initializer input exercises optional defaulting before map-character validation: fg/filling default ROOM25, bg defaults STONE0 in mazegrid. This does not establish all optional readers or callbacks. Required totterrain leading-NUL rejects in the control; do not globally collapse required and optional behavior.",
      "No tree, object, monster, bridge or player runtime behavior; stop before finalization. Shipped exposure and score relevance unknown. This is one existing C-string-prefix cause with five additional paths, not five new repairs or a broad equivalence proof.",
      "Deferred/unexecuted in this family: mazewalk typ downstream construction, optional fromterrain empty/mapfragment fallback, other init styles, function-valued string readers, general options/alignment/class/name strings, non-ASCII coercions. Prior Main-owned terrain/map witnesses and all parked/denied work remain untouched."
    ]
  },
